From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "NickLabs Orbis (port)" <orbis@nicklabs.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:02:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: PS4 SMU mailbox (expert interface, opt-in)

rmux's Liverpool SMU7-style mailbox driver (linux-psx 7.2-ps4 0167, GPL-2.0-only):
SMC indirect register read, mailbox command submission and the community-identified
memory P-state messages (0x57/0x58/0x59). Ported to 6.15; the sysfs files
(liverpool_smu_cmd, liverpool_smu_mempstate, liverpool_smu_reg) exist only with
amdgpu.ps4_smu_mailbox=1. The message semantics are community research, not vendor
documentation; Orbis userspace reads it only for diagnostics and never writes on its own.

Status: applies; not compiled or tested on hardware.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/Makefile        |   2 +-
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/cik.c           |   2 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/liverpool_smu.c | 257 +++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/liverpool_smu.h |  34 +++
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/inc/amdgpu_dpm.h    |   1 +
 5 files changed, 295 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/liverpool_smu.c
 create mode 100644 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/liverpool_smu.h

